# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, CORRECT.
#
# The Dockerfile installs dependencies for linux/amd64 (`npm install`) and
# then does `COPY . .`. Without this file the host's node_modules is copied
# straight over the freshly installed ones -- on a Windows or macOS host that
# means @esbuild/win32-x64 and @rollup/rollup-win32-* land in a Linux image
# and the Vite build fails or silently uses the wrong binary. Excluding
# node_modules is a correctness requirement here, not an optimisation.
#
# It also takes the context from ~304 MB to a few MB.

node_modules
dist
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Secrets never belong in a build context. VITE_* values that the bundle
# genuinely needs are passed explicitly as --build-arg by the CI workflow.
.env
.env.*

# Local tooling and editor state
.vscode
.idea
*.log
.DS_Store
.eslintcache

# Docs do not affect the bundle
*.md
